# memory-zero — reference env (copy to config/.env)
# M9 engine: single data/memory.db (SQLite + FTS5, no daemon).
# The embedding stack (QDRANT_*, EMBEDDING_*, LLAMA_SERVER_URL) is GONE —
# nothing reads those vars anymore (config.py keeps inert defaults).

# Project root. Everything lives inside it (env_loader contract).
MEMORY_SERVER_DIR=/Users/manu/.mcp-agent-memory

# Paths (defaults relative to MEMORY_SERVER_DIR; override only if needed)
# VAULT_PATH=$MEMORY_SERVER_DIR/data/vault
# STAGING_BUFFER=$MEMORY_SERVER_DIR/data/staging_buffer

# Identity (M4/strict): agent id only — the token NEVER lives in this file.
# ⚠️ Partial credentials kill ANY boot (ISO-14 fail-closed), even in open
# mode: never set MEMORY_AGENT_ID here without the token. Pass the id inline
# to the config generator instead:
#   MEMORY_AGENT_ID=pi-agent scripts/generate-mcp-config.sh --install
# 1. Register once (prints the token):
#      scripts/register_agent.py register pi-agent
# 2. Store it in the macOS Keychain:
#      security add-generic-password -s "memory-zero/pi-agent" -a "$USER" -w '<token>'
# 3. Regenerate the client config (see step 3 above).
